    {
      "page_title": "Delivery Semantics: The Three Guarantees",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Guarantees",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Semantic",
            "Loss",
            "Duplicates"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "at-most-once",
              "possible",
              "impossible"
            ],
            [
              "at-least-once",
              "impossible",
              "possible"
            ],
            [
              "exactly-once",
              "none",
              "no dup effect"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "at-most-once: delivered zero or one time",
            "at-least-once: delivered one or more times",
            "exactly-once: exactly one observable effect"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "A Pipeline Property"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Spans produce + store + consume + side effects",
            "No single config flag grants it",
            "Two halves: producer-to-broker, consumer commit",
            "Each half is chosen independently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "produce",
              "store",
              "consume",
              "side effect"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The pipeline guarantee is the weakest of its links. An at-least-once producer plus an at-most-once consumer is at-most-once end to end."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Where Dupes And Loss Are Born"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Duplicates: retry after an ambiguous outcome",
            "Write committed, ack lost on the wire",
            "Loss: acking before the data is durable",
            "Loss: committing progress before processing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "The Retry Dilemma",
          "text": "On timeout you retry and risk a duplicate, or you don't and risk loss. Only deduplication escapes both."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Kafka Actually Dodges"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "EOS = exactly-once processing inside Kafka",
            "Not exactly-once delivery over a network",
            "Two-generals limit dodged with idempotence",
            "Ordering is a separate axis from count"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Pick By Workload",
          "items": [
            "Metrics, logs, traces: at-most-once is fine",
            "Billing, ledgers: exactly-once or idempotent sink",
            "Everything else: at-least-once, dedup at the sink"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Semantic",
            "Mechanism",
            "Cost"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "at-most-once",
              "fire-and-forget",
              "cheapest"
            ],
            [
              "at-least-once",
              "ack + retry",
              "modest"
            ],
            [
              "exactly-once",
              "retry + dedup",
              "coordination"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The acks Knob",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "acks",
            "Waits for",
            "Failure mode"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`0`",
              "nothing",
              "silent loss"
            ],
            [
              "`1`",
              "leader log write",
              "loss if leader dies"
            ],
            [
              "`all` / `-1`",
              "all in-sync replicas",
              "stall, not loss"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Producer Durability: acks, min.insync.replicas & Retries",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`acks=0` never waits for a broker response",
            "`acks=1` replies before followers replicate",
            "`acks=all` is required for any at-least or exactly claim"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Durability Needs Two Settings"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`min.insync.replicas` is a broker/topic setting",
            "`acks=all` with `min.insync.replicas=1` still loses",
            "Standard: RF=3, `min.insync.replicas=2`, `acks=all`",
            "Tolerates one broker loss without loss or stall"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "var tp = new TopicPartition(t, p);",
            "var off = new OffsetAndMetadata(",
            "    rec.offset() + 1);  // +1 mandatory",
            "consumer.commitSync(Map.of(tp, off));"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Loud Beats Silent",
          "text": "`NotEnoughReplicasException` fires when in-sync replicas fall below `min.insync.replicas`. The producer stalls instead of losing data quietly."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Timeouts And Retries"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`retries` defaults to `Integer.MAX_VALUE` now",
            "`delivery.timeout.ms` (120000) is the real deadline",
            "`retry.backoff.ms` spaces the attempts",
            "`request.timeout.ms` bounds one attempt, not the send"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Duplicates Start Here",
          "items": [
            "Broker commits the batch",
            "Ack is lost on the wire",
            "Producer resends the same batch",
            "Partition now holds it twice"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "In-Flight And Ordering"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`max.in.flight.requests.per.connection` > 1 reorders",
            "Batch 2 lands, batch 1 retries in after it",
            "Idempotence keeps 5 in-flight safe and ordered",
            "Keep `unclean.leader.election.enable=false`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Unclean election lets an out-of-sync replica become leader and truncate committed data. Silent loss dressed as availability."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Check Your Callback"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "producer.send(record, (meta, ex) -> {",
            "  if (ex != null)",
            "    handleFailure(record, ex); // else lost",
            "});"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An ignored async exception is at-most-once",
            "`enable.idempotence=true` is default since 3.0",
            "It implies `acks=all`, retries>0, in-flight<=5",
            "A conflicting value now fails config validation"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "11",
              "12",
              "13",
              "14",
              "15"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [],
            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "last 5 seq per (PID, partition)"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Idempotent Producer: PIDs, Costs & the Guarantee Ladder",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Goal Of Idempotence",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Make a producer retry a no-op on the broker",
            "At-least-once delivery, exactly-once writes",
            "Enable with `enable.idempotence=true`",
            "On by default in Kafka 3.0+"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "PID And Sequence Numbers"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Broker assigns a PID via `InitProducerId`",
            "Every batch stamped (PID, epoch, base sequence)",
            "Sequence rises monotonically per partition",
            "An epoch bump fences an older zombie instance"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "InitProducerId",
              "get PID",
              "stamp seq",
              "broker checks",
              "append or dedup"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Fatal, Don't Retry",
          "items": [
            "`ProducerFencedException`",
            "`OutOfOrderSequenceException`",
            "Authorization errors",
            "Close the producer instead"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What Each Rung Costs"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Setting",
            "Overhead"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`acks=0` → `all`",
              "+ slowest ISR hop"
            ],
            [
              "idempotence",
              "low single-digit %"
            ],
            [
              "transactions",
              "~3-20% throughput"
            ],
            [
              "small txns",
              "hurt most"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`linger.ms` and `batch.size` matter more for throughput",
            "Batching amortizes every per-request cost",
            "`compression.type=lz4`/`zstd` works per batch",
            "Bigger batches compress better"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Producer-Side Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`acks=all` with `min.insync.replicas=1`",
            "`unclean.leader.election.enable=true` for \"HA\"",
            "Ignoring the `send()` callback exception",
            "`max.in.flight`>1 without idempotence reorders"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Cheapest Big Win",
          "text": "Turn on ==idempotence== and set `min.insync.replicas=2`. Near-zero cost, removes the most common duplicate and loss paths."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Guarantee Ladder"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "no acks",
              "acks=all",
              "idempotence",
              "transactions",
              "read_committed"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Idempotence kills producer-retry duplicates",
            "Transactions kill partial writes",
            "`read_committed` kills aborted reads",
            "Each rung fixes a **different** failure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Duplicates showed up — whose fault?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Same offsets: consumer-side redelivery",
            "Different offsets: producer-side resend"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Sequence Dedup Limits & What an Offset Is",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Incoming seq",
            "Broker action"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "<= last",
              "success, no append"
            ],
            [
              "last + 1",
              "append"
            ],
            [
              "> last + 1",
              "`OutOfOrderSequenceException`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Duplicate detection is silent dedup",
            "A gap means a batch was permanently lost",
            "Broker holds the state in a producer snapshot"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Scope Limits"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Dedup is per (PID, partition), per session",
            "Restart the process: new PID, dedup window gone",
            "`transactional.id` makes the PID stable",
            "Covers broker-side retries only"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "cloud",
          "title": "Not Your App's Dedup",
          "text": "Idempotence removes duplicates the client created on retry. Calling `send()` twice yourself writes two records."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "State And Overhead"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`producer.id.expiration.ms` default 86400000",
            "Idle producer state ages out on the broker",
            "Cost: a few bytes per batch plus broker state",
            "Effectively free next to transactions"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two Traps",
          "items": [
            "No cross-partition atomicity at all",
            "A two-partition send can half-succeed",
            "High partition counts grow producer-state memory",
            "Watch brokers holding many idle PIDs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "qa",
          "q": "Idempotence is on — am I exactly-once?",
          "a_bullets": [
            "Per partition, per session: yes",
            "Across partitions: no, you need transactions",
            "Across a restart: no, you need `transactional.id`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What An Offset Is",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A position per (topic, partition)",
            "Committed offset = next record to read",
            "Not the last record read — hence the +1",
            "Stored in compacted `__consumer_offsets`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "That internal topic is keyed by (group, topic, partition). Compaction keeps only the latest position per key."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Commit Timing Picks The Semantic"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "cards",
          "spec": {
            "cards": [
              {
                "title": "Commit then process",
                "lines": [
                  "crash skips records",
                  "at-most-once",
                  "you chose loss"
                ]
              },
              {
                "title": "Process then commit",
                "lines": [
                  "crash replays batch",
                  "at-least-once",
                  "you chose dupes"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Auto-Commit & Consumer-Side Pitfalls",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Auto-Commit Is Subtler"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`enable.auto.commit=true` commits inside `poll()`",
            "Every `auto.commit.interval.ms`, default 5000",
            "Commit fires on the next poll: at-least-once",
            "Hand off to a thread and return: at-most-once"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Consumer-Side Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Committing before processing \"to avoid dupes\"",
            "Auto-commit left on in a transactional app",
            "Slow batches blowing `max.poll.interval.ms`",
            "Fix: smaller `max.poll.records`, or worker + `pause()`"
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Retention Looks Like Loss",
          "text": "Retention or compaction can delete records before a ==lagging consumer== reads them. The data is gone, not undelivered."
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Monitor These",
          "items": [
            "Consumer lag",
            "LSO lag",
            "Transaction abort rate",
            "Producer `record-error-rate`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Commit Patterns, Rebalances & Transaction Basics",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Blocks",
            "Retries"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`commitSync()`",
              "yes",
              "retriable errors"
            ],
            [
              "`commitAsync()`",
              "no",
              "never"
            ],
            [
              "later commit",
              "-",
              "supersedes it"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Standard Commit Pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "try { for (var r : records) process(r);",
            "      consumer.commitAsync(); }",
            "finally { consumer.commitSync();",
            "          consumer.close(); }"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rebalance And Reset"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`auto.offset.reset` applies with no valid offset",
            "`latest` silently skips an entire backlog",
            "Rebalance re-delivers uncommitted records",
            "A rebalance mid-batch is a duplicate factory"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Two Hooks To Wire",
          "items": [
            "`onPartitionsRevoked`: last chance to commit",
            "`max.poll.interval.ms` default 300000",
            "Exceed it: kicked out, `CommitFailedException`",
            "The batch is then reprocessed by the new owner"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "What A Transaction Buys",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Writes across many partitions, atomically visible",
            "Offset commits join the same atomic unit",
            "Solves consume-transform-produce",
            "Outputs and input offsets land together or not at all"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Producer Lifecycle"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "initTransactions",
              "beginTransaction",
              "send",
              "sendOffsets",
              "commit"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`initTransactions()` once, at startup",
            "`transactional.id` unique per logical instance",
            "It must be stable across restarts",
            "The feeding consumer needs `enable.auto.commit=false`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "java",
          "lines": [
            "producer.beginTransaction();",
            "results.forEach(producer::send);",
            "producer.sendOffsetsToTransaction(",
            "    offsets, groupMeta);",
            "producer.commitTransaction();"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "On Exception",
          "text": "Any throw in the block means `abortTransaction()` and reprocess. `ProducerFencedException` is fatal — exit, never retry."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Paying For Transactions"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Cost is per transaction, **not** per record",
            "Two extra coordinator round trips each",
            "Plus one control marker per touched partition",
            "Streams commits every ~100ms by default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "transactional.id Traps",
          "items": [
            "Shared across instances: mutual fencing loop",
            "Random at startup: fencing breaks",
            "Then the old zombie keeps writing"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Transaction Coordinator & Two-Phase Commit",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Coordinator And Two-Phase Commit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "One coordinator per `transactional.id`",
            "Chosen by hashing into `__transaction_state`",
            "Writes `PREPARE_COMMIT` first",
            "Then control markers to every touched partition",
            "Then `COMPLETE_COMMIT`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Hidden Broker Load"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`__transaction_state` is a real, replicated topic",
            "So is `__consumer_offsets` — extra write load",
            "Memory grows with live PIDs and open transactions",
            "Many short-lived producers is an anti-pattern"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Rebalances Get Pricier"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Guarantee",
            "Throughput",
            "Safety"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "at-most-once",
              "highest",
              "lowest"
            ],
            [
              "at-least-once",
              "~95%",
              "no loss"
            ],
            [
              "exactly-once",
              "80-95%",
              "full"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Decision Guide",
          "text": "Under EOS a rebalance aborts open transactions. Start with ==at-least-once + idempotent sink==; use transactions only when the sink can't be made idempotent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Isolation Levels & the Last Stable Offset",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Markers Cost An Offset",
          "items": [
            "Control batches live in the partition log",
            "They consume a real offset",
            "So committed offsets show visible gaps"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Timeouts And Fencing"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Setting",
            "Default",
            "Bounds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`transaction.timeout.ms`",
              "60000",
              "one transaction"
            ],
            [
              "`transaction.max.timeout.ms`",
              "900000",
              "broker ceiling"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The client value must be <= the broker ceiling",
            "`initTransactions()` bumps the epoch",
            "Older producer, same id: `ProducerFencedException`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Where It Stops",
          "items": [
            "Kafka-to-Kafka only",
            "An external DB write is not covered",
            "Streams: `processing.guarantee=exactly_once_v2`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Isolation Knob",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Level",
            "Sees aborted?",
            "Sees open?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`read_uncommitted`",
              "yes",
              "yes"
            ],
            [
              "`read_committed`",
              "no",
              "no, waits"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`read_uncommitted` is the default, always",
            "It shows records the instant they are written",
            "Even ones a later abort throws away",
            "Without `read_committed` the machinery buys nothing"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Last Stable Offset"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "LSO = offset of the earliest still-open transaction",
            "A `read_committed` consumer never reads past it",
            "One long transaction blocks that partition",
            "Committed records queued behind it wait too"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "array",
          "spec": {
            "cells": [
              "100 done",
              "101 done",
              "102 open",
              "103 open",
              "104 open"
            ],
            "indices": true,
            "pointers": [],
            "highlight": [],
            "dim": [],
            "caption": "log, LSO stuck at 102"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Client-Side Filtering"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Broker ships an aborted-transaction index per fetch",
            "The client drops aborted batches before your code",
            "Control markers never surface as records"
